	)
	(text "GPIO5/GPIO6 SPI-mode strap pull-downs (R10-R17, added in a later pass): the real\nQorvo DWM3000 Data Sheet Rev B, May 2021 (already cited above) explicitly shows, in\nboth Figure 1 'Timing diagram for cold start POR' and Figure 2 'Timing diagram for\nwarm start', a 'Sample GPIOs 5&6 to set SPI mode' step during the AON power-up\nsequence, before the digital core reaches its active states. Table 2 'Pin Descriptions'\nconfirms GPIO5/EXTTXE/SPIPOL (pin 10) and GPIO6/EXTRXE/SPIPHA (pin 9) 'act as the\nSPIPOL/SPIPHA pin for configuring the SPI mode of operation' on power-up, defaulting\nto General Purpose I/O afterward. Section 6.3 'GPIO and SPI I/O Internal Pull Up /\nDown' confirms all GPIOs default to an internally SW-controllable pull-down (10k-30k,\nvarying with VDD1), which already yields SPI mode 0 (SPIPOL=0, SPIPHA=0) by default --\nbut per this task's explicit ask, each anchor gets its own EXTERNAL 10k pull-down on\nboth pins (R10/R11 for U4, R12/R13 for U5, R14/R15 for U6, R16/R17 for U7) to make\nSPI mode 0 a defined hardware default rather than relying solely on the internal\npull across 4 separate remote anchor boards. All 8 placed explicitly (not compacted\ninto a single shared note) for consistency with this sheet's existing per-anchor-\nexplicit-component convention (each anchor already gets its own full decoupling set,\nC8-C19, rather than a single shared/implied passive)."
		(at 60 240 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "2ef21d2a-b7d5-4fb1-98c3-3ff28956d768")
	)
